-- title:
--   Grid reading of the Gauss-order difference at scale e'
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible element $\varpi$, let $e_w,e_K\ge 1$, $e=e_we_K$, and $e'\ge 1$. Work in `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ^e)`, the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1-\varpi^e$. Two nonzero elements $x,x'$ are given together with normal-form data: pairs $ab=(a,b)$, $ab'=(a',b')$ of one-variable power series with $b(0)=b'(0)=0$ whose images `inU a + inV b` (the series supported on the $X_0$-axis resp. the $X_1$-axis) reduce to $x$ resp. $x'$. Write $v_r(w)=r\cdot\mathrm{addVal}_W(w)$ in $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$. The hypothesis `hagree` requires that for all $r\ge 1$ and $0<s<r(e'e)$ with $s$ not of the form $r(e'e-de_K)$ for some $d\le e'e_w$, the circle index drops of $ab$ and $ab'$ at weight data $(v_{re'},\,re'e,\,s)$ coincide; here the index drop is $\sup-\inf$ of the set of $n\in\mathbb{Z}$ whose term order $v(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,n)+\mathrm{annulusWeight}$ attains the representative Gauss order of `inU a + inV b`. Let $\varphi(t)$ be the difference of the `toNat` of the Gauss orders (suprema over lifts of the representative Gauss orders) of $x$ and $x'$ at $(v_{e'},e'e,t)$, and $G(d)=(\varphi(e'e-de_K)-\varphi(e'e))/e_K$. The conclusion asserts: $e_K\mid\varphi(e'e-de_K)-\varphi(e'e)$ for all $d\le e'e_w$; for $1\le d<e'e_w$ the second difference $(G(d)-G(d-1))-(G(d+1)-G(d))$ equals the difference of the index drops of $ab$ and $ab'$ at $(v_{e'},e'e,e'e-de_K)$; $G(1)-G(0)$ equals minus the difference of the suprema of the dominant index sets at $(v_{e'},e'e,e'e)$, and also equals $-(\varphi(e'e)-\varphi(e'e-1))$; and $G(e'e_w)-G(e'e_w-1)$ equals minus the difference of the infima of the dominant index sets at $(v_{e'},e'e,0)$, and also equals $-(\varphi(1)-\varphi(0))$. All subtractions of naturals are truncated.
--
--   This is the grid reading of the difference of Gauss orders on the $e'$-fold subdivided depth grid of the crossing model: under the assumption that the index drops of the two normal forms agree off the subdivided grid, the difference $\varphi$ is affine between consecutive grid indices, and the normalised function $G$ records its second differences at interior grid points and its two end slopes. It is the scale-$e'$ form of the integral-depth statement, obtained from [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq), and is used in the analysis of prolongation tuples at a place specialisation, namely by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_slopeDrop_eq_sum_div_depth_of_yDepth_pow_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_slopeDrop_eq_sum_div_depth_of_yDepth_pow_eq).
